<article class="env-definition" id="06BZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BZ">Definition <span data-tag="06BZ">76.47.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>perfect</em> if the equivalent conditions of Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03MJ" data-tag="03MJ">67.22.1</a> hold with $\mathcal{P} =$“perfect”. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $x \in |X|$. We say $f$ is <em>perfect at $x$</em> if there exists an open neighbourhood $X' \subset X$ of $x$ such that $f|_{X'} : X' \to Y$ is perfect. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>